---
title: Build info - Vintage Story Wiki
description: What commit/CI run generated this build, and how long each pipeline phase took.
layout: layouts/base.njk
permalink: "{{ lang }}/build/index.html"
---
{% import "macros/breadcrumb.njk" as bc %}
{{ bc.trail(lang, [{label: "Build info"}]) }}
<h1>Build info</h1>
<p class="muted">
  Full detail behind the "generated X ago" note in the footer of every page: exactly which
  commit/branch/CI run produced this build, and how long each of the three pipeline phases
  (download, ingest, site build) took to run.
</p>

<h2>This build</h2>
{% if buildInfo.isCi %}
  <div class="card">
    <p>
      Built in GitHub Actions from
      {% if buildInfo.repoSlug %}<code>{{ buildInfo.repoSlug }}</code>{% endif %}
      {% if buildInfo.branch %} on branch <code>{{ buildInfo.branch }}</code>{% endif %}.
    </p>
    <p>
      Commit:
      {% if buildInfo.commitUrl %}<a href="{{ buildInfo.commitUrl }}"><code>{{ buildInfo.commitShortSha }}</code></a>{% elif buildInfo.commitSha %}<code>{{ buildInfo.commitShortSha }}</code>{% else %}unknown{% endif %}
      {% if buildInfo.commitMessage %} &mdash; {{ buildInfo.commitMessage }}{% endif %}
      {% if buildInfo.commitAuthor %} (<span>{{ buildInfo.commitAuthor }}</span>){% endif %}
    </p>
    {% if buildInfo.runUrl %}<p>CI run: <a href="{{ buildInfo.runUrl }}">{{ buildInfo.runUrl }}</a></p>{% endif %}
    <p>
      Generated
      <time datetime="{{ buildInfo.utcIso }}" data-build-time="{{ buildInfo.utcIso }}">{{ buildInfo.utcIso }}</time><span data-build-ago> ago</span>
      (<code>{{ buildInfo.utcIso }}</code> UTC).
    </p>
  </div>
{% else %}
  <p class="wip-badge">Local build &mdash; no CI metadata available</p>
  <div class="card">
    <p class="muted">
      This build did not run in GitHub Actions, so the <code>GITHUB_SHA</code>/
      <code>GITHUB_REPOSITORY</code>/<code>GITHUB_RUN_ID</code> environment variables Actions sets
      automatically on every run aren't present, and there's no CI run to link to. The fields
      below are resolved from the local git working tree instead (best-effort, and may be absent
      too, e.g. outside any git repo at all):
    </p>
    <p>
      Repo: {% if buildInfo.repoSlug %}<code>{{ buildInfo.repoSlug }}</code>{% else %}unknown{% endif %}
      &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp;
      Branch: {% if buildInfo.branch %}<code>{{ buildInfo.branch }}</code>{% else %}unknown{% endif %}
    </p>
    <p>
      Commit:
      {% if buildInfo.commitUrl %}<a href="{{ buildInfo.commitUrl }}"><code>{{ buildInfo.commitShortSha }}</code></a>{% elif buildInfo.commitSha %}<code>{{ buildInfo.commitShortSha }}</code>{% else %}unknown{% endif %}
      {% if buildInfo.commitMessage %} &mdash; {{ buildInfo.commitMessage }}{% endif %}
      {% if buildInfo.commitAuthor %} (<span>{{ buildInfo.commitAuthor }}</span>){% endif %}
    </p>
    <p>
      Generated
      <time datetime="{{ buildInfo.utcIso }}" data-build-time="{{ buildInfo.utcIso }}">{{ buildInfo.utcIso }}</time><span data-build-ago> ago</span>
      (<code>{{ buildInfo.utcIso }}</code> UTC).
    </p>
  </div>
{% endif %}

<h2>Pipeline timings</h2>
<p class="muted">
  Each phase below runs as its own process (in CI, three separate workflow steps, possibly
  minutes apart) and persists its own timing to a small JSON file under
  <code>site/_data/generated/</code> that this page reads &mdash; see
  <code>src/ingest/types.ts</code>'s <code>DownloadTiming</code>/<code>IngestTiming</code>/
  <code>EleventyBuildTiming</code> for the exact shape of each.
</p>

<h3>1. Download (<code>npm run download</code>)</h3>
{% set dl = generated.downloadTiming %}
{% if dl.finishedAtIso %}
  <div class="card">
    <p>Took <strong>{{ dl.durationMs | durationLabel }}</strong>, finished <code>{{ dl.finishedAtIso }}</code> UTC.</p>
    <p>
      {% if dl.anyDownloaded %}
        <span class="tag tag-positive">freshly downloaded</span> at least one of the server/mods was actually fetched this run.
      {% else %}
        <span class="tag">already present</span> everything was cached from a previous run (skip-checked, not re-fetched) &mdash; a small duration here is expected, not a bug.
      {% endif %}
    </p>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>What</th><th>Outcome</th><th>Took</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Vintage Story server</td><td>{{ dl.serverAction }}</td><td>{% if dl.serverDurationMs != null %}{{ dl.serverDurationMs | durationLabel }}{% endif %}</td></tr>
        {% for mod in dl.modActions %}
          <tr><td>{{ mod.modid }}</td><td>{{ mod.action }}</td><td>{% if mod.durationMs != null %}{{ mod.durationMs | durationLabel }}{% endif %}</td></tr>
        {% endfor %}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
{% else %}
  <p class="card muted">Not available &mdash; <code>npm run download</code> hasn't been run yet in this checkout (or ran before this feature existed).</p>
{% endif %}

<h3>2. Ingest (<code>npm run ingest</code>)</h3>
{% set ing = generated.ingestTiming %}
{% if ing.finishedAtIso %}
  <div class="card">
    <p>Took <strong>{{ ing.durationMs | durationLabel }}</strong>, finished <code>{{ ing.finishedAtIso }}</code> UTC.</p>
    {% if ing.steps.length %}
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Step</th><th>Took</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        {% for st in ing.steps %}
          <tr><td>{{ st.name }}</td><td>{{ st.durationMs | durationLabel }}</td></tr>
        {% endfor %}
      </tbody>
    </table>
    {% endif %}
  </div>
{% else %}
  <p class="card muted">Not available &mdash; <code>npm run ingest</code> hasn't been run yet in this checkout.</p>
{% endif %}

<h3>3. Site build (Eleventy)</h3>
<p class="muted">
  Eleventy can't report its own total duration to its own templates &mdash; the number isn't
  known until the process is already exiting, after every page (including this one) has already
  rendered. <code>scripts/build-site.ts</code> wraps the real <code>eleventy</code> CLI, times the
  whole child process, and writes <code>eleventyBuildTiming.json</code> only after it exits. That
  means the figure below is always <strong>one full build run stale</strong>: it describes the
  previous successful build, not the one that produced this page. It is shown here labeled as
  such rather than silently presented as a live number.
</p>
{% set ev = generated.eleventyBuildTiming %}
{% if ev.finishedAtIso %}
  <div class="card">
    <p>
      Previous build took <strong>{{ ev.durationMs | durationLabel }}</strong>, finished
      <code>{{ ev.finishedAtIso }}</code> UTC.
      {% if not ev.succeeded %}<span class="warning">That build did not complete successfully.</span>{% endif %}
    </p>
  </div>
{% else %}
  <p class="card muted">
    Not available &mdash; the site hasn't been built via <code>scripts/build-site.ts</code> yet
    (e.g. a bare <code>npx eleventy</code> invocation was used instead, or this is the very first
    build in this checkout).
  </p>
{% endif %}
